otengine/godot/pull/121176.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121176.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121184\r\n\r\nWhen the game window is shrunk down, the scene tree is difficult to view due to being squished. This especially happens on Wayland when the window spawns next to the editor, causing the editor to get constrained horizontally.\r\n\r\nThe main issue was the controls in the 2D, 3D, and script view taking up a ton of space horizontally, so switching from `HBoxContainer` to `HFlowContainer` fixes this. They overflow in a new row now\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c2e6add5-e425-47df-8d84-f399b61c006f\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter (Even by default when the new window spawns there is more space horizontally):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/59066d36-de95-4b0a-883c-a9fd25e98e7f\r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nMost of the changes are renames. \r\n\r\nFor the script tab this PR only changes the \"online docs\" and \"search help\" buttons to be in an HFlow.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121176/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}